-Latest Mission 03/04 local validation: `make -j2`, combiner/vertex-stream/scissor adapter tests, and ASan/UBSan tests pass. The Metal backend now uses three in-flight vertex/depth slots with bounded non-overlapping vertex slices, plus correctly clipped top-left-origin scissors; these source-reviewed fixes remain unverified by Apple's compiler/GPU. A clean overlay materialization at commit `79ef8cda` passed focused and sanitized tests and linked the full Linux executable; the subsequent scissor update is pending rematerialization. SDL preparation and Linux CMake checks pass. Overlay workflows `45730350990`, `45730896116`, and `45731814680` were rejected before any runner steps because GitHub reports failed account payments or a spending-limit restriction; no Apple compilation or IPA exists. Continue local parity work and rerun when GitHub can allocate runners.
+Latest local source checkpoint is `1d2498f99b1235f0df4f47b7034ae04192d28e40` (tree `8103ebc2bc6b4340a51cfd0ba7d8daf8a67b4688`). Host `make -j2`, adapter/combiner tests, and ASan/UBSan tests pass. The exact private overlay materialization passed a clean Linux link plus focused and sanitized tests. Metal now uses three in-flight vertex/depth slots with non-overlapping, bounded vertex slices and correctly clipped top-left-origin scissors. These are source-reviewed and host-logic-tested fixes, not Apple-compiled or GPU-verified behavior. Overlay workflows `45730350990`, `45730896116`, `45731814680`, and `45732668194` were rejected before runner steps because GitHub reports account payment/spending-limit restrictions; Apple compilation and IPA remain blocked. Continue parity work and rerun after the account-level runner block is cleared.
